fixed non-ortho basis stuff


Here are details of the changes and rationale. I've run four sanity checks:
1. basis vectors and angles are consistent with box/system output
~kmclaugh/testing/v118-ortho/kays_test
2. energies scale correctly for non-ortho boxes (when the system is replicated in each direction)
~kmclaugh/testing/v118-ortho/checkEnergysanity/3D-chain-basis
3. an identical system represented via conventional unit cell and skewed (non-ortho) cell produce the same energies
~kmclaugh/testing/v118-ortho/checkEnergysanity/3D-chain-basis  and ~kmclaugh/testing/v118-ortho/checkEnergysanity/3D-chain-basis-conventional
4. nearest image distances are being properly calculated
~kmclaugh/testing/v118-ortho/checkEnergysanity/checkpairsep (with the aid of a debugger to check the value of system->molecules->atoms->pairs->rimg



Be wary of the histogramming for non-ortho boxes. I've made modifications consistent with the changes in other portions of the code, so I think it's fine, but I've not run any tests. The same is true for cavity insertion. These are probably fine to use, but use them with caution and double-check your work (and MPMC's work).


.........


A lot of problems have arised from the incorrect treatment of basis-vector multiplication. In MPMC,
the reciprocal basis matrix consists of column vectors. The basis matrix, on the other hand, are row vectors. This is normal,
so that the matrix multiplication of basis * recip yields the identity matrix (basis_vector dot reciprocal_vector = kronecker delta)

99% of the time when you do a multiplication of the basis or reciprocal basis matrix times a vector v, v represents the weight
of each vector. Thus, basis*v should be written 
result[p] = basis[q][p]*v[q]
That is, we count each row vector basis[q] a number of times equal to v[q].
Reciprocal vector * v should be written
result[p] = recip_basis[p][q]*v[q]
because we count each column vector recip_basis[][q] a number of times equal to v[q]


I've attempted to make all neccessary modifications to the code (rev 119). I've also documented all the checks I've performed (in cases where checks were actually performed). 
You should read over these changes, understand them, and make sure they are correct/make sense/etc. I've done my best to ensure these changes (and non-changes) are correct, but
I give no guarantee to their accuracy. This business can be tricky. Use at your own risk.


../energy/pairs.c:211:			img[p] += system->pbc->reciprocal_basis[p][q]*d[q];
../energy/pairs.c:219:			di[p] += system->pbc->basis[p][q]*img[q];
>		should be  //  out[p] += basis[q][p]*in[q] //
		in[q] is a vector that contains the amount of times to allow each basis vector basis[q] contribute to di[p]
		note that we have out[p] and in[q], not out[p] and in[p]
		> this change was tested ( see ~kmclaugh/testing/v118-ortho/checkpairsep )


