../energy/lj.c:211:										a[p] += system->pbc->basis[p][q] * i[q];
> changed to [q][p]

>> energy is tested between identical systems, but one specified in a non-ortho unit cell (but equivalent). energies are pretty much exact with the exception of a slight difference in polarization energy, which is almost definitely due to cutoff effects (it seems to converge aas the system size is increased. those testing data are located in ~kmclaugh/testing/v118-ortho/checkEnergysanity/3D-chain-basis and ~kmclaugh/testing/v118-ortho/checkEnergysanity/3D-chain-basis-conventional

