>> not positive about these as I'm not familiar with the cavity code, use at own risk:

../mc/cavity.c:69:				pos_vec[p] += system->pbc->basis[p][q]*grid_vec[q];
> changed. this is evident because pos_vec[x] should be equal to only x-contributions of the basis times some quantity (we aren't performing a rotation, AFAIK). the x-components of basis[p][q] are basis[p][0], so pos_vec[0] += basis[p][0] * grid_vec[p].

../mc/cavity.c:165:						grid_vector[p] += system->pbc->basis[p][q]*grid_component[q];
> changed. same logic as above.

../mc/cavity.c:170:						grid_vector[p] -= 0.5*system->pbc->basis[p][q];
> changed. same logic.

../mc/mc_moves.c:634:						com[p] += system->pbc->basis[p][q]*rand[q];
> changed. same logic.

